    "Scouting Notes": "Swing is pretty flat, could use just a little better attack angle in order to lift the ball more\n Little more swing and miss than I had anticipated\n Lifting the ball more will be important, as there is some raw power there\n Like the hit tool in general, but will be interested to see if the whiff is an issue, it got much better as the season progressed\n Overestimated the ability to stick in center, though he does get good reads and takes solid routes, the athleticism is more solid than great\n Not a great basestealer, both in terms of instincts and speed.\n Super young, very mature approach and also seems like a very mature player and person\n Type of guy you bet on the refined skills and IQ, while the skills are more solid than great",
